&#x20;
            },\
&#x20;     {\
&#x20;       "id": "item-combat-chassis",\
&#x20;       "name": "Combat Chassis Prototype II",\
&#x20;       "quantity": 1,\
&#x20;       "description": "Functioning nonmagical bilateral greatblade-gauntlet system, worn in the normal configuration. G1 RIGHT accommodates Blood, while G2 LEFT accommodates Bleed. Allows Kael to wield two full-sized 2d6 greatswords without reducing their damage dice. Compatible with Relentless Assault and Bleed's cascade-maintenance conditions. Grants no independent attack, action, Bonus Action, Reaction, AC, Strength, attack bonus, free energy, or enchantment. Swords normally retract into their respective forearm gauntlets when stowed."\
&#x20;
            },\
&#x20;     {\
&#x20;       "id": "item-blood",\
&#x20;       "name": "Blood — Ancestral Edge",\
&#x20;       "quantity": 1,\
&#x20;       "description": "Kael's original self-forged ancestral full-sized greatsword, fitted to the RIGHT G1 gauntlet. NONMAGICAL. Attack +9, ordinary damage 2d6+5 Slashing. Eligible Attack-action Heavy-weapon hits gain Great Weapon Master's +4 damage. May qualify for Relentless Assault's separate +4 damage. Has Graze mastery. Can maintain Bleed's primed cascade through a successful greatsword hit, but cannot spend Bleed charges, advance powered stages, or deal Bleed Force damage. No +1 enhancement or independent impulse reservoir."\
&#x20;
            },\
&#x20;     {\
&#x20;       "id": "item-bleed",\
&#x20;       "name": "Bleed — Magic Greatsword",\
&#x20;       "quantity": 1,\
&#x20;       "description": "Attuned magical full-sized greatsword fitted to the LEFT G2 gauntlet. NOT a +1 weapon. Attack +9 and ordinary damage 2d6+5 Slashing. Eligible Attack-action Heavy hits gain Great Weapon Master's +4; qualifying alternating hits may gain Relentless Assault's separate +4. Has Graze mastery. Maximum three charges, restored on a qualifying Long Rest; actual current remaining charges are unverified. Kael may voluntarily spend one charge on a successful Bleed hit for an additional powered Force-damage stage: first +1d6 Force, second +2d6 Force, third +3d6 Force and a conditional DC 15 Strength save against displacement. Powered-stage maintenance and reset follow the established cascade rules. Bleed requires attunement, and Kael is currently attuned."\
&#x20;
            },\
