&#x20;       "name": "Relentless Assault",\
&#x20;       "description": "CURRENT APPROVED HOMEBREW FIGHTING STYLE, replacing Great Weapon Fighting. Prerequisite: Fighting Style feature. While wielding two Greatswords using a compatible combat chassis, when Kael hits a creature with one of those weapons as part of the Attack action on his turn, that attack deals additional nonmagical Slashing damage equal to his Proficiency Bonus (+4) if his immediately preceding attack on that turn was a hit with the OTHER Greatsword made as part of an Attack action. Targets may differ. The benefit can occur multiple times, including across separate Attack actions on the same turn. Movement between attacks does not interrupt a valid chain. A missed attack interrupts it; a Graze result on a miss is not a hit. Attacking again with the same sword does not itself gain the bonus, though that hit can serve as the preceding attack for a subsequent opposite-sword hit. An intervening different attack can change the immediately preceding attack. Hew Bonus Action attacks, Riposte Reaction attacks, and Opportunity Attacks do not trigger or maintain the Attack-action-only chain. The +4 is flat nonmagical Slashing damage and does not double on a critical hit. Example: Blood hit, Bleed hit, Blood hit gives bonuses 0, +4, +4. Six consecutive alternating eligible Attack-action hits using Action Surge can yield five +4 bonuses, totaling +20. Grants no additional attacks, actions, reactions, AC, mobility, speed, magic, charges, or ability score increases. Kael does NOT retain the former Great Weapon Fighting damage-die floor.",\
