&#x20;       "name": "Bleed — Powered Force Cascade",\
&#x20;       "description": "Established homebrew mechanics for Kael's attuned magical greatsword Bleed. Maximum three charges; replenish on a qualifying Long Rest. Current remaining charges and powered stage are not independently certified by this permanent base sheet. When Kael successfully hits with Bleed, he MAY voluntarily expend one charge to produce the current powered-stage effect. First consecutive powered stage: +1d6 Force damage, then stage 2 is primed. Second: +2d6 Force, then stage 3 is primed. Third: +3d6 Force; if the target is Large or smaller, it must succeed on a DC 15 Strength saving throw or Kael may push it up to 10 ft directly away. The cascade then resets to stage 1. While Kael wears a functioning Combat Chassis Prototype II in its established dual-greatsword configuration, the powered cascade remains primed if he lands at least one hit with either Blood or Bleed on each of his turns. A Blood hit may maintain the stage but cannot spend a charge, deal Force damage, or advance the stage. Missing with one sword does not reset it if the other greatsword hits on that turn. Ending a turn without a successful hit from either greatsword resets the cascade to stage 1. The cascade also resets after the third powered hit or loss or ending of a valid attuned operating state. Only charge-spending Bleed hits advance the powered stage. Normal Bleed hits do not automatically spend charges. The added Force damage dice double on an applicable critical hit, while ordinary flat modifiers do not. Normal legal expenditure within the three-charge maximum does not require an invented automatic wear check. Bleed is magical; Blood is nonmagical.",\
