&#x20;   "notes": "SOURCE AND SCOPE: This conversion represents Kael Veylor's permanent, unrestricted Fighter 11 base character sheet from the owner-approved CP40-qualified record. It does NOT represent a temporary scene-specific character profile, suppressed ability set, altered level, reduced maximum HP, or current initiative tracker. The underlying CP40 and some recent checkpoint sources are SOURCE-COVERAGE PARTIAL / EVIDENCE-LIMITED. Actual subsequent gameplay changes take precedence. Creating or importing this record does not create a rest, restore resources, activate equipment, move the character, or advance game time.\n\nCURRENT HP WARNING: Maximum HP is confirmed as 90. The source's 90/90 is explicitly a FULL-HEALTH REFERENCE BASELINE, not certification of the actual HP remaining after CP40 events. Therefore currentHp 0 is an unknown-value placeholder, NOT a claim that Kael is unconscious, dying, or at zero HP. The exact present HP must be obtained from the controlling live scene. Likewise temporaryHp 0 is a placeholder because no present Temporary HP amount is certified, not proof of the current live amount.\n\nHIT DICE: Maximum 11d10 at Fighter 11. Actual remaining or spent Hit Dice are not independently established in this base sheet. Follow the applicable 2024 Long Rest recovery rules. Do not infer that all eleven Hit Dice are available.\n\nNORMAL RESOURCE MAXIMUMS, NOT CURRENT COUNTS: Second Wind maximum 4 uses; Action Surge maximum 1; Superiority Dice maximum 5d10; Indomitable maximum 1; Know Your Enemy free use maximum 1 per Long Rest; Heroic Inspiration normally maximum 1; Bleed maximum 3 charges; attunement capacity 3, all occupied. Actual remaining Second Wind uses, Action Surge, Superiority Dice, Indomitable use, Know Your Enemy use, Heroic Inspiration, Bleed charges, and active cascade stage are NOT certified by this base document. The reference values 4/4, 1/1, 5/5, 1/1, 1/1, and 3/3 are FULLY RESTORED EXAMPLES, not evidence of a completed rest or current availability. Short and Long Rest recharge must follow actual played time and the applicable feature rules. Bleed charges recover on qualifying Long Rests; Superiority Dice recover on Short or Long Rests; Know Your Enemy has one free use per Long Rest; Human Resourceful grants Heroic Inspiration after Kael's own Long Rest.\n\nPASSIVE SCORES: Normal Passive Perception 16; Passive Insight 16; Passive Investigation 15. Passive sight-based Perception is 21 only while Eyes of the Eagle are actually worn and their benefits apply.\n\nSAVING THROWS: Strength +9 proficient; Constitution +6 proficient; Dexterity +0, Intelligence +1, Wisdom +2, and Charisma -1 not proficient.\n\nSKILL PROFICIENCIES: Arcana +5, Athletics +9, Insight +6, Investigation +5, Nature +5, Perception +6, Persuasion +3, Religion +5, Survival +6. No Expertise is established. Human Skillful provides Perception; Human Versatile and Skilled provide Arcana, Nature, Religion; Student of War provides Insight. Other proficiencies come from the established class/background build. Chain Mail imposes Disadvantage on Stealth checks even though Stealth's ordinary modifier remains +0.\n\nWEAPON AND ARMOR PROFICIENCIES: All Simple and Martial weapons. Light, Medium, and Heavy Armor and Shields.\n\nTOOL PROFICIENCIES: Five confirmed: Smith's Tools, Leatherworker's Tools, Tinker's Tools, Woodcarver's Tools, and Jeweler's Tools. Smith's Tools example check modifiers include Intelligence +5 and Strength +9 when applicable; Jeweler's Tools Intelligence +5 when applicable; the other named proficient tools use the relevant ability modifier plus proficiency bonus +4. Mason's Tools proficiency is explicitly NOT established. Smith's Tools and Jeweler's Tools have certified physical sets. The other three Crafter tool proficiencies do NOT automatically create physical equipment.\n\nLANGUAGES: Common, Talarin, Dwarvish.\n\nCARRYING CAPACITY: Kael's normal Medium-creature Strength 20 carrying capacity is 300 lb. Push, drag, or lift capacity is 600 lb under the same general rule unless additional restrictions apply. These are physical capacity limits, not proof that all owned items or stored materials are being carried.\n\nCOMBAT DCs: Battle Master maneuver save DC 17. Normal Strength-based 2024 Unarmed Grapple and Shove save DC 17, subject to legal reach, free-hand, target-size, and saving throw requirements. Grappling or shoving does not automatically deal weapon attack damage.\n\nATTACK ACTION ECONOMY: Three attacks per Attack action at Fighter 11. Action Surge may grant another eligible non-Magic action, potentially producing three additional attacks. Ordinary greatsword damage on hit is 2d6+5 Slashing with +9 attack bonus. For qualifying Attack-action Heavy hits, Great Weapon Master increases this to 2d6+9 Slashing. A separately qualifying Relentless Assault follow-up hit increases it by another +4, giving 2d6+13 Slashing. Bleed may additionally spend a charge for the relevant powered-stage Force damage. None of these situational bonuses is automatically added to every attack. The attack entries record ordinary damage to avoid counting conditional bonuses twice. A normal critical hit doubles applicable damage dice, including greatsword weapon dice, relevant Superiority damage dice, and Bleed Force dice, but not flat Strength, Great Weapon Master, or Relentless Assault modifiers.\n\nRELENTLESS ASSAULT QUALIFICATIONS: The CURRENT Fighting Style is Relentless Assault, an approved campaign homebrew replacement for Great Weapon Fighting. The old Great Weapon Fighting damage-die floor is not active. A successful alternating Blood/Bleed Attack-action sequence can accumulate separate +4 Slashing bonuses only if the immediately preceding attack on the same turn hit with the other greatsword as part of an Attack action. A miss interrupts the sequence; Graze on a miss remains a miss. Same-sword repeated hits do not themselves trigger the bonus, though they can serve as the immediately preceding hit for a later other-sword attack. Hew, Riposte, and Opportunity Attacks do not trigger or maintain the chain. The bonus is nonmagical, flat, and not doubled on critical hits.\n\nBLEED MECHANICS AND ATTUNEMENT: Blood is Kael's NONMAGICAL ancestral greatsword. Bleed is a separate MAGICAL greatsword with maximum three Long Rest-recharging charges, a voluntary charge-spending Force cascade, and an established conditional DC 15 Strength save after the third powered hit against a Large-or-smaller target. Bleed is not a +1 weapon. Blood hits can preserve the powered cascade but do not advance it or deal Force damage. Both require the functioning dual-greatsword chassis configuration for the established cascade-maintenance interaction. No independent chassis attacks, offhand attacks, or energy are created.\n\nATTUNEMENT: All three normal attunement slots are occupied by Bleed, Cloak of Displacement, and Wings of Flying. Eyes of the Eagle does NOT require attunement. The four magic items are owned and physically retained/restored through the CP40 record. Ownership and attunement do not automatically certify that the Cloak is currently worn, Wings are actively deployed, Eyes are currently worn, or any scene-specific item effect is currently functioning. Do not break or change attunement because a temporary event held or suppressed an owned object.\n\nEQUIPMENT WEAR AND ACTIVATION: Chain Mail provides normal AC 16 and Stealth Disadvantage. Cloak of Displacement requires actual wear and operative status for its defensive illusion. Wings of Flying require actual wear and a Magic action for activation, with a 60-ft Fly Speed for up to an hour and a 1d12-hour reactivation delay after disappearance. Eyes of the Eagle require actual wear for sight-related benefits. Their current wear, deployment, suppression, and cooldown states must be confirmed from live play.\n\nSTOREROOM C CUSTODY: Kael has a rented, locked compartment, Storeroom C, at the Gilded Pike North Quay Annex in Darsenne. The original rental payment was 8 gp for a 30-day term with a separate 2 gp refundable key deposit. The current live rental expiration is NOT independently certified. Stored materials are separate from carried encumbrance. Stored Galeb Duhr materials total 58 lb: two cores weighing 50 lb, two pieces of enchanted pumice totaling 4 lb, and two Motes of Earth totaling 4 lb in enchanted vials. Other stored material includes Umber Hulk parts, Behir lightning sack, Hydra blood, Shambling Mound parts, Bulette claws, Giant Boar tusks, hide, Owlbear liver, Giant Spider silk gland, Ettercap poison, and Old Saffron basilisk teeth. The four Bulette claws have a historically unresolved shared-title ownership issue; exclusive Kael ownership must not be assumed. Earlier Owlbear feathers and neck material are under separate historical Beldrin Ashlace custody in Ridgegate. The removed maker's G1 blade and prepaid compact B-01 pair remain separately Korga-held. None of these off-person possessions is automatically in Kael's carried inventory.\n\nHISTORICAL EQUIPMENT COUNTS: Original Dungeoneer's Pack contents were backpack, caltrops, crowbar, two oil flasks, ten ration-days, rope, tinderbox, ten torches, and waterskin. These are historical starting quantities, not a guaranteed current stock. Nine NEW ration-days totaling 18 lb are separately confirmed. The current remainder of previous rations, torches, oil, consumables, and some older gear is not freshly recertified. Inventory quantity 0 for a historically established but uncounted item indicates UNKNOWN current quantity, not confirmed non-possession. Do not silently restore starting consumables or assume omitted mundane possessions were lost.\n\nCURRENCY: Latest owner-approved CP40 personal purse is exactly 198 gp, 0 sp, 0 cp. Previously paid storeroom rental and separately refundable key deposit are historical transactions, not an instruction to subtract those amounts again. No further current debt is certified in this base handoff. Do not invent financial obligations or payments.\n\nABILITIES AND PROGRESSION: Fighter 4 selected Great Weapon Master with Strength increasing to 18 during established progression. Fighter 6 raised Strength by 2 to 20. Fighter 8 increased Wisdom from 13 to 15. Fighter 11 provided the third Attack-action strike and established Relentless Assault as the current Fighting Style. Seven known Battle Master maneuvers are retained. No additional Fighter 11 maneuver, feat, class, or unselected future option should be fabricated.\n\nSPELLCASTING: No spellcasting ability, spells, cantrips, or spell slots are provided by the established Fighter 11 build. Wings of Flying requires a Magic action, but this does not grant spell slots or permit Action Surge to take the Magic action. No spell entries are confirmed.\n\nSOURCE LIMITATIONS: The CP40 source is partly evidence-limited. This character record intentionally excludes temporary stage-specific suppression, unverified current remaining resources, undocumented new powers, a fabricated item-by-item current weight census, uncertain consumable balances, undocumented document custody, and unsupported new equipment. Later actually played events supersede this reference where properly documented. Permanent capabilities are not proof of active scene effects. No time, rest, healing, recovery, equipment movement, purchase, or progression occurs by generating this JSON.",\
